# ignore every review artifact — peer/, archive/, scoped/, and any dir added later
#
# .why = the harness ROTATES finished reviews out of peer/ into archive/. an ignore
#   scoped to peer/ alone is therefore correct at write time and DEFEATED the moment a
#   review is archived — the file moves from an ignored path to an unignored one, and
#   ~800 llm transcripts become sweepable by `git add -A`.
#
# .note = this sits at the .reviews/ ROOT on purpose, so every subdir inherits it and no
#   new dir the harness invents can reopen the same gap.
*
!.gitignore
